          "Arm: the horizontal distance from the datum to the item's CG — positive aft of the datum, negative forward. A 'station' (flight station, FS) is the same thing: FS 50 = 50 in aft of datum. Large holds and cabins are given an AVERAGE (centroid) arm.",
          "Moment: mass × arm — the turning effect of a mass about the datum (e.g. 100 lb × 20 in = 2 000 in-lb). Large moments are divided by a reduction factor (100, 1 000, 10 000) to give an INDEX (Moment/100). The same factor must be used throughout.",
